          "guid": "mt7le493r8li3kjc",
          "message": {
            "text": "Private-domain calls and teardown are hard-bounded because an inspector traversal or crashed renderer can otherwise strand the evidence worker indefinitely. Timeout and teardown errors use fixed safe labels and are discarded without interpolating protocol payloads, preserving the denied-body non-serialization boundary even on failure.",
            "markdown": "Private-domain calls and teardown are hard-bounded because an inspector traversal or crashed renderer can otherwise strand the evidence worker indefinitely. Timeout and teardown errors use fixed safe labels and are discarded without interpolating protocol payloads, preserving the denied-body non-serialization boundary even on failure."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "tools/animated-image-owner-resource-truth-collector.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 143,
                  "endLine": 184,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "async function bounded<T>(\n  operation: Promise<T>,\n  milliseconds: number,\n  safeLabel: string,\n): Promise<T> {\n  let timeout: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | undefined;\n  try {\n    return await Promise.race([\n      operation,\n      new Promise<never>((_resolve, reject) => {\n        timeout = setTimeout(\n          () => reject(new Error(safeLabel)),\n          milliseconds,\n        );\n      }),\n    ]);\n  } finally {\n    if (timeout) clearTimeout(timeout);\n  }\n}\n\nasync function sendPrivate<T>(\n  cdp: CDPSession,\n  method: \"DomotionAnimatedImageTruth.begin\" |\n    \"DomotionAnimatedImageTruth.finish\",\n  params: Record<string, unknown>,\n): Promise<T> {\n  return await bounded(\n    cdp.send(method as never, params as never) as unknown as Promise<T>,\n    PRIVATE_PROTOCOL_TIMEOUT_MS,\n    \"bounded private protocol timeout\",\n  );\n}\n\nasync function boundedTeardown(operation: Promise<unknown>): Promise<void> {\n  try {\n    await bounded(operation, TEARDOWN_TIMEOUT_MS, \"bounded teardown timeout\");\n  } catch {\n    // Teardown diagnostics must not replace the already sealed failure stage,\n    // and protocol errors may contain resource facts. Discard them entirely.\n  }\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
